welcome to the workflow debugging shell

1. you're currently in your workflow's working directory. if you used 'actions/checkout'
   you will find your repo content here.

2. everything related to your workflow can be found in:

   ls <RUNNER_HOME>/_work

3. all your workflow steps (and all bash steps from the actions you 'use')
   can be found in:

   ls <RUNNER_HOME>/_work/_temp

4. every bash step is located in a separate, uuid-named file.
   to find the step you want to debug, list all step files with:

   tail -n +1 <RUNNER_HOME>/_work/_temp/*sh

5. you can also change a step file and run it again.

6. logs of your workflow can be found in:

   ls <RUNNER_HOME>/_diag

7. to print the log of the steps that ran so far use:

   cat -n <RUNNER_HOME>/_diag/blocks/$(ls -S <RUNNER_HOME>/_diag/blocks/ | head -n 1)

8. when you are done, log out to end the shell session and the workflow continues.
   if you set `continue=false`, run this instead:

   touch $HOME/action_continue && exit

have fun!
